# 🔥 MobiGo Auth Service — Revision Part 2
# Problems, JS vs TS, Type System & Interview Questions

---

## 🐛 Problems Jo Tumhe Aayi Thi & Solutions

### Problem 1: `Cannot find module '../models/User.js'`
```
❌ import {IUser} from "../models/User.js";  // "models" folder nahi hai!
✅ import {IUser} from "../model/User.js";   // "model" folder hai!
```
**Seekh:** Import path me folder/file ka naam EXACT match hona chahiye.

---

### Problem 2: `Property 'user' does not exist on type 'Request'`
**Kyu aaya?** Express ka default [Request](file:///c:/Users/rajni/mobigo/services/auth/src/middlewares/isAuth.ts#5-8) type me `user` property nahi hai.
Humne khud [isAuth.ts](file:///c:/Users/rajni/mobigo/services/auth/src/middlewares/isAuth.ts) me `req.user = decodedToken.user` set kiya, par TS ko pata nahi!

**Solution:**
```typescript
// isAuth.ts me custom type banaya:
export interface AuthenticatedRequest extends Request {
    user?: IUser | null;  // Ab Request me user property aa gayi!
}

// Controller me use kiya:
export const addUserRole = TryCatch(async (req: AuthenticatedRequest, res) => {
    req.user?._id  // ✅ Ab error nahi aayega!
});
```

---

### Problem 3: `error is of type 'unknown'`
**Kyu?** TypeScript strict mode me catch ka error `unknown` type hota hai.
```typescript
// ❌ Error:
catch(error) { console.log(error.message); }  // 'unknown' pe .message nahi

// ✅ Fix:
catch(error: any) { console.log(error.message); }  // any = kuch bhi allowed
```

