## ⚔️ JavaScript vs TypeScript — Complete Comparison

### 1. Basic Farq
| Feature | JavaScript (JS) | TypeScript (TS) |
|---------|-----------------|-----------------|
| Type System | ❌ Nahi (Dynamic) | ✅ Hai (Static) |
| Error Detection | Runtime pe (App crash) | Compile time pe (Code likhte waqt) |
| File Extension | `.js` | [.ts](file:///c:/Users/rajni/mobigo/services/auth/src/index.ts) |
| Browser Samjhe? | ✅ Directly | ❌ Pehle compile → JS |
| Learning Curve | Easy | Thoda mushkil initially |

### 2. Code Examples se samjho:

**Example 1: Variable Types**
```javascript
// JavaScript — Koi bhi type daal do, koi nahi rokta
let age = 25;
age = "twenty five";  // ✅ Chal jayega! (Bug ka raasta)
age = true;           // ✅ Ye bhi chal jayega!
```
```typescript
// TypeScript — Guard baitha hai
let age: number = 25;
age = "twenty five";  // ❌ ERROR: Type 'string' is not assignable to 'number'
age = true;           // ❌ ERROR!
```

**Example 2: Function Parameters**
```javascript
// JavaScript — Galat data bhejo, crash runtime pe hoga
function greet(name) {
    return "Hello, " + name.toUpperCase();
}
greet(42);  // ✅ No error likhte waqt... ❌ CRASH runtime pe!
// TypeError: name.toUpperCase is not a function
```
```typescript
// TypeScript — Galat data bhejne hi nahi dega
function greet(name: string): string {
    return "Hello, " + name.toUpperCase();
}
greet(42);     // ❌ COMPILE TIME ERROR! (App crash se bacha liya)
greet("Rajni"); // ✅ "Hello, RAJNI"
```

**Example 3: Object Shape**
```javascript
// JavaScript — Object me kuch bhi add/remove karo
const user = { name: "Rajni", age: 22 };
console.log(user.email);  // undefined (Error nahi, par galat result)
user.xyz = 123;           // ✅ Naya property add ho gayi!
```
```typescript
// TypeScript — Object ka shape fix hai
interface User { name: string; age: number; }
const user: User = { name: "Rajni", age: 22 };
console.log(user.email);  // ❌ ERROR: Property 'email' does not exist
user.xyz = 123;           // ❌ ERROR!
```

